WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.430
Of all the deadliest, nastiest, most monstrous
creatures contained by the SCP Foundation,

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.389
there is none quite like SCP-682.

00:00:08.389 --> 00:00:16.660
A mean, green, perpetual motion killing machine,
this beast runs on spite and unnatural strength,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.680
fueled by hatred and an unslakable thirst
for violence.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:25.880
With no known way of permanently destroying
the thing, SCP-682 is likely to remain in

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.830
Foundation custody until the sun burns out.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.910
Unless, of course, the research staff can
finally crack the code on killing the thing

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:33.920
once and for all.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.200
But one scientist at the SCP Foundation couldn't
help but wonder: did violence really have

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.700
to be the answer?

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.370
Was the only way to manage SCP-682's hateful
heart to stop it from beating?

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:51.360
Dr. Bright was having his weekly movie night,
joined this time by SCP-507, who loved a good

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.500
film whenever he was in a dimension that happened
to have them.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:59.680
He had campaigned for a viewing of "The Avengers,"
but Dr. Bright insisted on something a little

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.220
more heartfelt.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.089
He remembered a book that his mother used
to read to him, and recalled that it had been

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:06.630
adapted into a movie.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:12.360
So, in spite of SCP-507's sulking, he pressed
play on "Black Beauty."

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.790
The story of a wild creature forming a bond
with a determined young girl, the two learning

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:21.470
and growing with each other and embarking
on an unlikely friendship, brought tears to

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.520
his eyes.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.000
If she could tame that wild stallion, then
why couldn't he, a man of infinite patience

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.520
and even more infinite time, try and tame
a wild beast of his own?

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.630
That settled it.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:37.450
He was going to take a stand, to try something
the Foundation had never dared attempt with

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.590
SCP-682.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.250
He was going to become its friend.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.670
"Are you out of your mind?!"

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.280
Dr. Gears nearly dropped his mug of plain
black coffee when Dr. Bright told him the

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.280
plan.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.369
"That thing will tear you limb from limb before
you can so much as say a word."

00:01:53.369 --> 00:01:54.869
"Then I'll get another body.

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:56.360
I'm willing to put in the work."

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:01.320
Dr. Bright shrugged, but as he looked at Dr.
Gears' look of deep concern, he decided that

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.909
it would be better to ask for forgiveness
than permission at this point.

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:06.979
He had to misdirect, and fast.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:07.979
"Ha!

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:10.270
I got you, look at your face!

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.010
That was a prank, I'm kidding, I would never
try that.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.959
Anyway, lots to do, bye!"

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:19.410
And he rushed off to undertake his grand vision
by himself.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.830
When it worked, then he could make the rounds
around the Foundation Site with his "I told

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:24.830
you so"s.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.780
Dr. Bright hadn't grown up on a horse ranch,
he hadn't even grown up with many pets.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.840
He had no idea where to begin when it came
to animal training, let alone the domestication

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.440
of highly intelligent, misanthropic, anomalous
animals.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.050
For an anomalous being, perhaps he needed
to try an anomalous method of taming it.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.200
Suddenly, it occurred to him: SCP-010!

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.989
That could work!

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:50.340
The iron collars were stored at Site-19, in
locked boxes.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:55.470
When worn, they would allow the wearer's every
movement to be controlled via a hand-held

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.470
remote.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.470
It was perfect.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:02.629
He could get SCP-682 to give him a hug, a
high-five, to learn choreographed dance routines

00:03:02.629 --> 00:03:06.019
they could perform together, the possibilities
were endless!

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:10.379
But when he went to access the locked storage
boxes, the guards posted outside the room

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:12.000
asked him what he was doing there.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.220
"Testing, it's all official," he said.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.630
But the guards insisted that they would have
been notified if any testing had been approved.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.140
He tried to argue with them, but as soon as
he saw their expressions turn suspicious,

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.400
he pivoted hard in a safer direction.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.610
"Just kidding!

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.610
Pranked.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.610
Got you good."

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.670
"Hah, yeah, you got us, Doc."

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.970
One of the guards forced a chuckle.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.620
"Stay safe out there!"

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.670
"Not if I see you first!"

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:40.400
Doctor Bright responded, realizing only later
that his response made no sense.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.170
Damn adrenaline, the thrill of the scheme
was making him loopy.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.099
He needed to center himself, to refocus and
figure out what his next step would be.

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:53.450
If the collar had any chance of working on
the massive reptile, the Foundation probably

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.540
would have tried it before...and if he tried
to sneak in and just steal one of the damn

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.379
things, someone might see him, then his plan
would be over before it even began.

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:09.760
Besides, he reminded himself, he was trying
to befriend SCP-682, not just pilot its movements

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.930
like some kind of giant remote-control toy.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:16.609
If it listened to him, it needed to be because
it wanted to.

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:20.260
Because they had formed a sacred bond between
man and beast.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.620
No, SCP-010 wasn't the answer.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:28.020
He needed to get the opinion of an expert,
hear advice from someone who really knew what

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.020
they were doing.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:33.830
He hopped online, and found exactly what he
was looking for: an online seminar on training

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.259
difficult animals.

00:04:35.259 --> 00:04:39.460
Okay, it was specifically a webinar about
obedience training for dogs with behavioral

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:45.520
problems, but what was SCP-682 if not a massive,
reptilian dog with a whole lot of behavioral

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:46.520
problems?

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:50.260
Besides, the webinar was only 50 dollars,
so really what could it hurt?

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:55.139
Dr. Bright kicked up his feet, poured himself
a drink, and tuned into the video seminar.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:58.699
Once the credit card payment went through,
and the five-hour session was through, he

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:03.990
would know exactly what to do to take SCP-682
from Keter to Cutie.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.479
Well, maybe that was a bit much.

00:05:06.479 --> 00:05:08.610
But stranger things happened every day.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:12.400
After all, he was a guy whose soul was trapped
in a necklace for all eternity.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.690
With a beeping sound, the live video began,
and Dr. Bright prepared to absorb all of the

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:21.270
wisdom Dr. Monique, PhD in Animal Psychology,
had to offer.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:25.470
He nodded off a few times, but for the most
part, he was able to retain some very valuable

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.470
tips.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.919
First, go slowly.

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:33.520
Start working with your dog (or giant anomalous
reptile) on familiar behaviors, or their favorite

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.900
things to do.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:39.160
Use positive reinforcement to encourage even
the smallest of successes.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.960
This will teach the pet that training is a
good thing.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.520
To ease the transition, only make one change
at a time.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.350
Next, control the environment.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:51.900
During training sessions, take away potential
distractions to help your pet stay focused.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:56.220
Put away toys they might be tempted to play
with (or things they might try to eat).

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:00.759
Minimize loud noises and other intrusions,
such as passing squirrels.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:05.410
Avoid punishment, as it can increase anxiety
and damage the relationship built on trust

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.790
between pet and owner.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:12.289
In the long term, punishment can serve to
increase aggression and other negative behaviors.

00:06:12.289 --> 00:06:18.030
Instead, use reward-based training tactics
based around things the pet wants and likes,

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:20.240
such as treats, petting, and playtime.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.620
When the pet does act out, redirect them to
a different behavior, then reward that.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.060
When doing reward-based training, however,
it's important to choose the right rewards.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:34.310
If the rewards aren't appealing, or given
frequently enough, they will stop evoking

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.580
the desired response in the animal.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:41.759
Every animal is different, so figure out what
yours loves and give them more of that.

00:06:41.759 --> 00:06:47.770
This particular tip might be hard to implement
for SCP-682, Dr. Bright thought as he wrote

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:48.770
it down.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:51.240
What do you give the anomaly that hates everything?

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.410
Still, he would figure it out.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:58.370
The final tips of note were to make training
a habit, part of the daily routine, made up

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.819
of short training sessions throughout the
day.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:04.560
If the training failed to produce desired
results, a reasonable pet owner should be

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.600
willing to bring in help from a trained expert.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:12.229
This is especially true if the animal is displaying
excessive aggression.

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:17.340
That one definitely applied to SCP-682, but
there was no one more qualified to handle

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:21.509
it than Dr. Bright was, in his own opinion
at least.

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:26.270
So, with no one else to call, he would have
to tackle the monumental undertaking himself.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:31.590
Dr. Monique concluded her seminar by asking
each attendee about their respective pets.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:36.940
Dr. Bright had to stretch the truth just a
little bit, responding only "a big one" when

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:42.740
asked about his dog's breed, and describing
its behavior problems as "aggression and biting."

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:46.200
"Well, troubled animals often just need a
little extra love and patience.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.030
And like I said, ask for help if you need
it!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:53.289
Good luck, Doctor," she said, giving him a
wave before he signed out of the meeting.

00:07:53.289 --> 00:07:57.740
So, armed with a can-do attitude, an open
heart, a spray bottle filled with hydrochloric

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:02.890
acid (just in case), some toys, and as much
sliced deli turkey as the local grocery store

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:08.229
would sell him, Dr. Bright prepared to sneak
into SCP-682's containment cell.

00:08:08.229 --> 00:08:12.930
He timed it perfectly, waiting for the shift
change so he could slip in unnoticed while

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.750
the guards were swapping out.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:18.419
Using moves he learned from watching dozens
of heist movies, he maneuvered around the

00:08:18.419 --> 00:08:23.530
security cameras, staying out of sight, and
let himself into the high-security containment

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:24.530
chamber.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:28.750
Dr. Monique said to remove all distractions
while training a pet, and the acid bath that

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:33.360
SCP-682 was submerged in was a pretty massive
distraction.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.860
How was Dr. Bright supposed to teach it anything
if the creature's attention was on the constant

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.810
corrosion of its flesh, muscle, and bone?

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:45.760
Good thing he paid attention during SCP-682's
official testing, and knew how to drain the

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.720
acid out of the room.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:53.200
As SCP-682's body began to rebuild itself,
it turned to look at Dr. Bright, eyes fixed

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.200
on him.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:59.010
It spoke, in a voice dripping with pure disdain:
"Why...did...you...do...that..."

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.700
"Hey buddy!"

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:07.090
Dr. Bright ignored the question, speaking
in a soft, higher-pitched voice that Dr. Monique

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:09.310
recommended for soothing troubled dogs.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.390
"Want a treat?"

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.600
He held out a pack of sliced turkey.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.710
Not waiting for an answer, he tossed the food
toward the reptile, and it landed just in

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:19.280
front of the creature's mouth with a soft
thud.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:25.089
After a moment of careful study, of making
sure this was not some sort of trick, SCP-682

00:09:25.089 --> 00:09:28.700
opened its mouth and swallowed the turkey
in one gulp.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:29.700
"More..."

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:33.320
It said, opening its mouth wide, exposing
its rows and rows of sharp teeth.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.380
"Wait a second.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.850
You can have more, but first...Sit!"

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.410
Dr. Bright held up his hand to teach the command.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:41.450
"Sssssit?"

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.360
The creature repeated, incredulous.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.360
"Sit!"

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.829
Dr. Bright repeated patiently.

00:09:46.829 --> 00:09:51.120
SCP-682 responded with a swipe of its tail
that knocked Dr. Bright into the wall, breaking

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.170
several of his ribs.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.170
"Bad 682!

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.170
Bad!"

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.959
Dr. Bright reflexively reached for the spray
bottle, squirting some acid onto the creature's

00:09:58.959 --> 00:09:59.959
scales.

00:09:59.959 --> 00:10:03.030
It recoiled, and Dr. Bright became aware of
what he was doing.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.510
He was using punishment when he should have
been using positive reinforcement.

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:09.550
He dropped the spray bottle, kicking it off
to the side.

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:12.760
"I'm so sorry buddy, that wasn't nice.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.550
I shouldn't have..."

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.930
SCP-682 wouldn't even look at him.

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:18.690
"Here, you want this?

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:19.690
Catch?"

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:21.870
He held up a large ball, tossing it toward
the creature.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.779
It bounced off the beast's nose uselessly.

00:10:24.779 --> 00:10:27.480
"Dissssgusssting." 682 growled.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.290
"You're right.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.290
That was disgusting.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.839
I forgot everything I learned, I let my ego
get in the way.

00:10:33.839 --> 00:10:37.010
Listen, I promise I'll never do it again."

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:41.930
He tossed more turkey toward the creature,
and, as it ate, he gently patted its broad,

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:42.930
scaly side.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:44.790
"I know you don't like my colleagues here.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.490
I get it, why would you?

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:50.070
They're always hurting you, trying to control
you...I know what that's like.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.910
We've got a lot in common, you know.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.260
We've both been through so much pain.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:57.120
We both can't die, even if we wanted to.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.959
If you let me, I could be a friend to you."

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:05.740
SCP-682 was silent for a moment as it stared
into Dr. Bright's eyes, considering his words.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:06.740
Then…

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.260
It spoke.

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:09.260
"You...are..."

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:14.230
Dr. Bright held his breath, waiting to hear
what came next.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.290
"Disssgusssting."

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:17.420
SCP-682 roared.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:21.670
The last thing Dr. Bright saw was the monster's
jaws clamping down around his head, and then

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:22.950
everything went black.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:27.840
Dr. Bright woke up in his office with that
stiff "new body" feeling he had become accustomed

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:28.840
to.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:32.430
There was a note waiting for him on his desk,
on the O5 Council's letterhead.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:33.430
It read:

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:34.430
"Dr. Bright.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:37.149
I hope you understand the gravity of what
you did today.

00:11:37.149 --> 00:11:41.720
Your careless actions caused a containment
breach of SCP-682 that resulted in over a

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.410
dozen casualties.

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:47.620
Be thankful you were given a new body at all,
as it was briefly debated whether or not you

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:48.709
deserved one.

00:11:48.709 --> 00:11:52.459
But you are too valuable to the Foundation
to keep locked in a box.

00:11:52.459 --> 00:11:53.600
Remember that.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:58.990
Do not interfere with SCP-682 again, or there
will be dire consequences.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:03.020
Additionally, as your viewing of Black Beauty
has been attributed to this incident, all

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:08.079
future film viewings must be subject to formal
approval, until you can prove that this is

00:12:08.079 --> 00:12:09.500
no longer necessary.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:13.220
Now sit in your office and think about what
you've done.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.220
- O5-1"

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.510
Dr. Bright slumped over his desk, feeling
sorry for himself.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:21.300
Suddenly, he heard a familiar cooing sound
coming from the doorway.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.449
He turned, and saw The Tickle Monster, here
to visit him and cheer him up.

00:12:25.449 --> 00:12:28.579
It oozed over to his desk, waiting for him
to pet it.

00:12:28.579 --> 00:12:31.880
As he patted its slimy surface, he smiled
to himself.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:36.180
No matter how many mistakes he made, how much
of a screwup he might feel like sometimes,

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:41.350
at least he knew SCP-999 would always be happy
to see him.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:45.370
Forget horses, dogs, and especially SCP-682.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.800
Man's Best Friend was right here.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:53.320
Now go check out “SCP-963 What Would You
Do If You Were Immortal Like Dr. Jack Bright?”

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:59.300
and “Could Dr Jack Bright Escape Silent
Hill?”

